{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Allon, son of Jeda[C]jah, stands in [Dm]the line
Father [Bbmaj7]of Shiphji, [C]his name is [Dm]divine
[Bb]No deed of [F]his hand [C]is written [Dm]in stone
[Bb]But in the ge[C]nealogy he is [Dm]known
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
They lived in Beersheba, Mola[C]dah, Haz-ar-[Dm]shual
In Bilhah, E[Bbmaj7]zem, To[C]lad, without [Dm]fail
Bet[Bb]huel, Hormah, [F]Ziklag, [C]the [Dm]towns
Where they [Bb]dwelt until [C]David, the king, was [Dm]found
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Their [Bb]villages E[C]tam, Ain, [Dm]Rimmon, and Tochen
With [Bb]Ashan, five [C]towns, the [Dm]record is spoken
A[Bb]round these [C]towns as [Am]far as [Dm]Baal
They [Bb]kept a genealog[C]ical record in the [Dm]hall
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
They went to the entrance of Ge[C]dor, east side of [Dm]the valley
To look for [Bb]pasture for [C]their flocks, steadi[Dm]ly
They [Bb]found rich, good [F]pasture, the [C]land was [Dm]broad
[Bb]Quiet and peace[C]ful, where the Hamites had trod
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Dm]In the days of [Bb]Hezekiah, they came [C]with might
At[Dm]tacked the tents, put [Bb]the Meunites [C]to flight
Destroyed [Dm]them completely, [Bb]so it re[C]mains
They [Am]settled in their [Dm]place, an[Bb]swering the chains
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[C]Recorded by name, in [Dm]the co[C]ve[Bb]nant [C]kept
